<title>UGANDA: Uganda steps up effort to combat coffee disease.</title>
<headline>Uganda steps up effort to combat coffee disease.</headline>
<dateline>KAMPALA 1997-04-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Uganda will spend $100,000 to counter a fungal coffee wilt disease that has affected at least 11 growing districts, officials of the state Uganda Coffee Development Authority (UCDA) said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>They said the money would come from the treasury under the coffee stabilisation tax or from the European Union (EU).</p>
<p>The disease, tracheomycosisis, is widespread in Bundibugyo, Kabarole and Rukungiri, UCDA officials said, adding that in other districts it was localised.</p>
<p>UCDA officials have said the disease is not yet considered a threat to Uganda's production.</p>
</text>
